meta {
  name: WatchEvents (streaming)
  type: grpc
  seq: 1
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.EventService/WatchEvents
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "since_event_id": ""
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  Live streaming of the account's events — it is where the timeline and the
  attention box come from.

  An empty `since_event_id` brings only what comes from here on. Filled in, the
  core DRAINS the log from that point and joins it to the live stream, with no gap
  and no duplicate.

  Isolation per account holds even for an event with a null account: it goes to
  nobody.

  A slow subscriber is dropped with `Unavailable` and the instruction to reconnect
  with a cursor — a client that does not consume cannot block the others.
}
